<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Garment Care Policy</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="../css/polos.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="../css/extra.css">
    <style>
    .care-policy-section {
        padding: 60px 20px;
        background-color: #ffffff;
        font-family: sans-serif;
    }

    .care-container {
        max-width: 1000px;
        margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .care-main-title {
        color: #008a45; /* Matching the green title in image_ee625c.png */
        text-align: center;
        font-size: 28px;
        margin-bottom: 50px;
    }

    .care-content {
        position: relative;
        padding-left: 30px;
    }

    /* Vertical Timeline Line */
    .care-content::before {
        content: '';
        position: absolute;
        left: 0;
        top: 0;
        bottom: 0;
        width: 2px;
        background-color: #000000;
    }

    .care-group {
        margin-bottom: 40px;
        opacity: 0; /* Base state for animation */
        transform: translateY(20px);
        transition: all 0.6s ease-out;
    }

    .care-group.visible {
        opacity: 1;
        transform: translateY(0);
    }

    .care-sub-title {
        color: #000000;
        font-size: 20px;
        margin-bottom: 15px;
        font-weight: bold;
    }

    .care-list {
        list-style: none;
        padding: 0;
    }

    .care-list li {
        color: #444444;
        font-size: 15px;
        line-height: 1.8;
        padding-left: 20px;
        position: relative;
        margin-bottom: 8px;
    }

    /* Custom Bullets */
    .care-list li::before {
        content: '•';
        position: absolute;
        left: 0;
        color: #000000;
        font-weight: bold;
    }
</style>
</head>

<body>

 <%- include('partials/nav') %>
    <section class="hero-section">
        <div class="hero-bg-container">
            <img src="../photos/hoodies.webp" alt="Vito and Will folded polo shirts" class="hero-image">
        </div>

    </section>
<section class="care-policy-section">
    <div class="care-container">
        <h2 class="care-main-title">All you Need to Know About Garments Care Policy</h2>

        <div class="care-content">
            <div class="care-group animate-on-scroll">
                <h3 class="care-sub-title">Washing Instructions</h3>
                <ul class="care-list">
                    <li>Wash garments inside-out with cold water cycle for longer durability.</li>
                    <li>Avoid bleach or harsh fabric softeners to maintain quality.</li>
                    <li>Flat drying or tumble dry with low heat prevents shrinkage.</li>
                    <li>Do not iron directly on printed or designed areas.</li>
                    <li>Strictly avoid dry cleaning to protect fabrics and prints.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="care-group animate-on-scroll">
                <h3 class="care-sub-title">Embroidered Apparel</h3>
                <ul class="care-list">
                    <li>Follow the care label instructions carefully for best preservation.</li>
                    <li>Wash inside-out on cold water cycle to maintain embroidery threads.</li>
                    <li>Avoid chlorine bleach, as it can cause discoloration of stitching.</li>
                    <li>Do not use fabric softeners, they damage embroidery durability.</li>
                    <li>Tumble dry on low heat or flat dry to prevent shrinkage.</li>
                    <li>Never iron directly on embroidered areas; iron inside-out only.</li>
                    <li>Dry cleaning is not recommended for embroidered items.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="care-group animate-on-scroll">
                <h3 class="care-sub-title">Heat-Pressed Vinyl</h3>
                <ul class="care-list">
                    <li>Treat vinyl prints the same way as screen printing for washing.</li>
                    <li>Do not use fabric softeners, as they weaken adhesive strength.</li>
                    <li>Wash inside-out with cold water to protect vinyl surface.</li>
                    <li>Tumble dry low or hang dry to avoid peeling of vinyl layers.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="care-group animate-on-scroll">
                <h3 class="care-sub-title">Fabric Softeners</h3>
                <ul class="care-list">
                    <li>Fabric softeners reduce cling and add softness, but avoid using them on:</li>
                    <li><strong>Screen Printed Shirts:</strong> They break down ink and fade the print.</li>
                    <li><strong>Vinyl Printed Shirts:</strong> Adhesive weakens, causing peeling.</li>
                    <li><strong>Polyester or Moisture-Wicking Fabrics:</strong> Leaves residue that reduces fabric performance.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="care-group animate-on-scroll">
                <h3 class="care-sub-title">General Apparel Care</h3>
                <ul class="care-list">
                    <li>Fabuluxe apparel is prewashed and preshrunk; avoid unnecessary shrink washing.</li>
                    <li>Excessive washing can fade both fabric and print quality.</li>
                    <li>Cotton-polyester blends shrink less, depending on polyester ratio.</li>
                    <li>Avoid dry cleaning as it can cause pilling from friction.</li>
                    <li>Pill-resistant yarn is used, but no fabric is 100% pill-free. Proper care extends garment life.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<%- include('partials/popup') %>
<%- include('partials/footer') %>
   <script>
    document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", function() {
        const observerOptions = {
            threshold: 0.2
        };

        const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
            entries.forEach(entry => {
                if (entry.isIntersecting) {
                    entry.target.classList.add('visible');
                }
            });
        }, observerOptions);

        const animatedElements = document.querySelectorAll('.animate-on-scroll');
        animatedElements.forEach(el => observer.observe(el));
    });
    
</script>
</body>

</html>